{"text": "1-800-HELP-FLA (435-7352)\nwww.800helpfla.com\nwww .freshfromflorida.com\n\nDIVISION OF CONSUMER SERVICES\n2005 APALACHEE PKWY\nTALLAHASSEE FL 32399-6500\n\nq\n\nSUR oa\n\nFLORIDA DEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE & CONSUMER SERVICES\nCOMMISSIONER ADAM H. PUTNAM\n\nDecember 5, 2013 Refer To: DTN2482490 CH35061\n\nSUNCOAST AQUATIC NATURE CENTER ASSOCIATES, INC.\n290 N CATTLEMEN RD\nSARASOTA, FL 34201\n\nRe: Application Under Solicitation of Contributions Act DTN: 2482490\nFirst Notice of Deficiency\n\nDear Applicant:\n\nThe Department received your application submitted under Chapter 496, Florida Statutes, the Solicitation of\nContributions Act. The application is deficient for the following reasons:\n\n1. You did not submit an acceptable financial report for your fiscal year ending 2012.\nFinancial information must be reported in one of the following formats:\na) The enclosed Financial Report form;\nb) IRS form 990 and Schedule A;\nc) IRS form 990EZ.\n\n2. Fee's will be caculated upon submission of the financials.\n\nPursuant to Chapter 496, Florida Statutes, this Notice is provided within 15 working days of receiving your\napplication to enable you to correct the cited deficiencies for further review by the Department. Your response\nto this letter should resolve each deficiency cited above; do not submit a partial response.\n\nIf you do not correct these deficiencies within 30 days from receiving this Notice your application will be denied\nand the Department will pursue its available legal remedies. Soliciting Contributions from persons in Florida, or\nfrom a physical location in Florida, without being properly registered is a violation of Chapter 496, Florida\nStatutes.\n\nThank you for your attention to this matter. If you have any questions regarding your application/filing, please\ncontact the undersigned at the number listed below.\n\nSincerely,\n\nAleta King\n\nAleta King\nRegulatory Consultant\n850-410-3715\nFax: 850-410-3804\naleta.king@freshfromflorida.com",
"words": [
